  "jei.impactscrafting.hold_time_range": "Hold for %s to %s",
  "jei.impactscrafting.info.beds": "Beds are built where they stand. Place a Bed Frame, right-click it with a Comforter, then with a Sheet: the sheet's color is the bed's. A sheet on a finished bed recolors it, and a broken bed drops all three parts.",
  "jei.impactscrafting.info.dye_vat": "Fill the vat with water from a bucket, or let rain fill it. One dye colors 8 dips, and a second dye mixes with the first when the colors mix (red and yellow make orange). Hold right-click with an item to dip it. Leather armor and packs take the vat's color; plain water washes dye off and soaks sugar cane into Paper Pulp.",
  "jei.impactscrafting.info.loose_items": "Unfinished items need their last step in hand: loose tools get their heads seated, riveted goods their rivets driven home, the piston its push rod fitted, all with a hammer (a pebble or the Iron Hammer) in your off hand; the blast furnace is sealed with Mortar instead. Hold the item in your main hand and hold right-click. Letting go early starts over.",
  "jei.impactscrafting.info.pebbles": "Pebbles are the first tool. Pick up the loose pebbles lying on grass, sand, stone and cave floors: their kind follows the ground (sandstone on sand, granite on granite). Breaking gravel drops one sometimes, and breaking stone by hand always does. Every kind works the same. A fresh pebble stacks to 64; once used, it stacks to 1.",
  "jei.impactscrafting.plain_water": "Plain water",
